WEBVTT

00:02:28.596 --> 00:02:32.236
There are several ways to break down
the sources of greenhouse gas emissions.

00:02:32.356 --> 00:02:35.116
Here we’re using the public
Climate Watch data.

00:02:35.876 --> 00:02:36.876
Start with energy.

00:02:37.076 --> 00:02:39.796
The majority of modern energy
comes from fossil fuels,

00:02:39.796 --> 00:02:43.556
which makes the energy sector
76 percent of the climate challenge,

00:02:43.556 --> 00:02:45.756
including the fuels
used for transportation,

00:02:45.756 --> 00:02:47.116
industrial processes

00:02:47.116 --> 00:02:48.516
and agricultural production.

00:02:48.996 --> 00:02:51.916
The shift to clean energy
must be accelerated

00:02:51.916 --> 00:02:53.716
by an order of magnitude

00:02:53.716 --> 00:02:58.316
if we want any chance to restrain
global warming to 1.5 degrees Celsius.

00:02:59.356 --> 00:03:02.036
And we’ll need more ways
to store this clean electricity,